rule c1xx: an out-of-line member definition reuses the function id its class declaration made, and costs its parameters, a re-declarator (a gap), `this` (unless static) and its exit label; a constructor's member initialisers cost nothing.
cl
il
  *#d5   #d6     25   0x10   16  ?k00@@YAHH@Z*
  *#ee   #dd      4   0x2b   43  ??0A@@QAE@H@Z                                formal 2, label 1, gap 1*
  *#f2   #df      4   0x1b   27  ?f@A@@QAEHH@Z                                formal 2, label 1, gap 1*
  *#f6   #e0      3   0x21   33  ?g@A@@QAEHXZ                                 formal 1, label 1, gap 1*
  *#f9   #e2      3   0x10   16  ?h@A@@SAHH@Z                                 formal 1, label 1, gap 1*
  *#fc   #e4      4   0x1b   27  ?v@A@@UAEHH@Z                                formal 2, label 1, gap 1*
  *#100  #101     4   0x37   55  ?k05@@YAHH@Z                                 fdef 1, formal 1, label 1, local 1*
  *#f2     formal     "q" level 1 [?f@A@@QAEHH@Z]*
